---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import { release, source } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy · Ostrilo"
  description="Ostrilo has no developer server, analytics, telemetry, or crash reporting. Learn what stays on your device and what goes to your chosen Nostr relays."
>
  <PageIntro label="Privacy" title="Your browser. Your data.">
    <p>
      The extension has no developer server and sends no analytics, telemetry, or crash reports to
      the developer. Here’s how it handles the data you choose to use.
    </p>
  </PageIntro>
  <div class="article-layout wrap">
    <nav class="page-index" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="section-label">Where data goes</p>
      <a href="#local">On your device</a>
      <a href="#network">Relays & websites</a>
      <a href="#website">This website</a>
      <a href="#policy">The full policy</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="prose">
      <section id="local">
        <h2>Kept in your browser.</h2>
        <p>
          The encrypted key vault, public keys and labels, permissions, relay addresses, settings,
          and activity records live in local extension storage. The browser may sync one preference:
          whether Ostrilo opens in the side panel.
        </p>
        <p>
          Private keys are encrypted. Activity records and settings are separate local data, and are
          not encrypted like the key vault. Activity includes the site origin, event kind, decision,
          and a content preview.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="network">
        <h2>Connections you can account for.</h2>
        <p>
          Ostrilo connects to your selected Nostr relays to fetch public profiles and publish
          profile changes. Relays receive the queried public keys and can see your IP address. The
          default relay is <code>wss://relay.primal.net</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Websites receive a public key with your consent and signed events you approve or permit
          through rules. Ostrilo returns website-requested signed events to the website. That
          website decides where to publish them.
        </p>
        <p>
          In extension {release.version}, profile images are not loaded from their remote hosts, and
          there’s no image-upload flow. Saving an image URL as profile metadata does not cause an
          image request from the extension.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="website">
        <h2>A quiet website, too.</h2>
        <p>
          This site contains no analytics, advertising, tracking cookies, remote fonts, or embedded
          third-party widgets. Fonts and images are served with the site. The signing walkthrough
          uses example data and never connects to your extension.
        </p>
        <p>
          The theme switch works within the current page without storing a preference. GitHub Pages
          hosts the website and receives ordinary web requests, including your IP address.{' '}
          <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
            GitHub’s privacy statement
          </a>{' '}
          covers its handling of that data.
        </p>
        <p>
          Following a link to GitHub, the Chrome Web Store, or another service takes you to that
          service, where its own privacy terms apply.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="policy">
        <h2>Read the extension’s full policy.</h2>
        <p>
          This page is a readable overview. The{' '}
          <a href={source('PRIVACY.md')}>extension privacy policy</a>, effective 6 October 2026, is
          the authoritative document for the extension. It covers storage, sync, files, clipboard,
          network use, permissions, and deletion.
        </p>
        <p>
          The website overview was reviewed on {release.reviewed}. Changes to extension data
          handling are recorded in the <a href={source('CHANGELOG.md')}>changelog</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
